  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "DEVSQ squares deviations with x87 multiplication and flushes subnormal squares to 0 before summing",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, DEVSQ computes the sample mean in binary64, forms each squared deviation RN53(RN64((v - mean) * (v - mean))) on the x87 unit, and flushes any subnormal square below DBL_MIN to 0 before summing (so DEVSQ(8.08239784871588e-295, 9.013847760079092e-295) returns 0). All 23,106 full-bank DEVSQ rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
